The implementation will work as follows:

* Success: When `bookShipmentGenerateLabel()` completes successfully, save the request and response with HTTP status `200`.

* Failure: If `bookShipmentGenerateLabel()` throws an exception, catch it, save the request and error details with the appropriate HTTP status, and rethrow the exception.

* Existing behavior: Keep the current SLF4J logging and API response handling unchanged.

* Database: Use the existing `cmsRecordUtil.saveRecord()` method without introducing another persistence method.

### Updated `shipmentBook()` controller method

```java

@PostMapping("/generatelabel")
public ResponseEntity<ShipmentBookResponse> shipmentBook(
        @RequestHeader HttpHeaders httpHeaders,
        @RequestBody @Valid ShipmentBookRequest shipmentBookRequest) {

    var requestId = MDC.get(ShipmentBookConstant.CORRELATION_ID);
    long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

    String urlPath = "/v1/api/cms/shipment/generatelabel";
    String source = shipmentBookRequest.getSource();

    log.atInfo()
            .addKeyValue(REQUEST_ID, requestId)
            .setMessage("Request to book shipment came for source : " + source)
            .log();

    try {
        ShipmentBookResponse shipmentBookResponse =
                shipmentBookService.bookShipmentGenerateLabel(
                        shipmentBookRequest, requestId, httpHeaders);

        log.atInfo()
                .addKeyValue(REQUEST_ID, requestId)
                .setMessage("Response for book shipment request for source : " + source)
                .log();

        // Persist successful generateLabel API response
        cmsRecordUtil.saveRecord(
                urlPath,
                HttpStatus.OK.value(),
                source,
                objectMapper.writeValueAsString(shipmentBookRequest),
                objectMapper.writeValueAsString(shipmentBookResponse),
                requestId,
                shipmentBookRequest.getFacilityId(),
                System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime
        );

        return new ResponseEntity<>(shipmentBookResponse, HttpStatus.OK);

    } catch (Exception ex) {

        log.atError()
                .addKeyValue(REQUEST_ID, requestId)
                .setCause(ex)
                .log("Failed to book shipment for source : {}", source);

        // Persist failed generateLabel API response
        try {
            cmsRecordUtil.saveRecord(
                    urlPath,
                    HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR.value(),
                    source,
                    objectMapper.writeValueAsString(shipmentBookRequest),
                    ex.getMessage(),
                    requestId,
                    shipmentBookRequest.getFacilityId(),
                    System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime
            );
        } catch (Exception loggingException) {
            log.error("Failed to persist generateLabel failure record",
                    loggingException);
        }

        throw new RuntimeException(ex);
    }
}
```

